sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant RD as R&D Team (Research)
    participant Ops as Ops, Accounts & Valuation
    participant PM as Portfolio Manager (PM)
    participant Dealer as Dealer Room (Trading)
    participant Custodian as Custodian, RTA & Market

    Note over RD, Custodian: Step 1-4: The Day's Collaborative Setup & Active Trading
    Ops->>PM: 1. Sends "Available Investable Cash" (09:00 AM)
    RD->>PM: 2. Shares buy/sell research and target ideas (09:15 AM)
    PM->>Dealer: 3. Decides & places trades via OMS (09:15 AM - 03:30 PM)
    Dealer->>Custodian: 4. Executes trades & reports daily fills/costs (09:15 AM - 03:30 PM)

    Note over Ops, Custodian: Step 5: Post-Market Reconciliation & Settlements (03:30 PM - 05:00 PM)
    Dealer->>Ops: Sends End-of-Day (EOD) trade allocations
    Custodian-->>Ops: Reconciles Daily trade settlements, contract notes, & cash flow statement (from RTA & Broker)

    Note over Ops, Custodian: Step 6: Closing Asset Valuation (05:00 PM - 06:30 PM)
    Custodian->>Ops: Provides the EOD Closing Stock/Debt prices (from NSE & BSE)
    Ops->>Ops: Marks-to-market (MTM) the stock portfolio's ending cash and equity/bond valuation

    Note over Ops, Custodian: Step 7: Ledger, Corporate Action & Fee Accruals (06:30 PM - 07:30 PM)
    Custodian->>Ops: Sends RTA unit balances (Daily subscriptions/redemptions & units issued)
    Ops->>Ops: Adjusts for corporate actions (dividends, interest earned) & deducts accrued Daily Expenses (Management fees, TER, & operating costs)

    Note over Ops, Custodian: Step 8-10: NAV Audit, Sign-Off & Distribution (07:30 PM - 10:00 PM)
    Ops->>Ops: NAV Calculation: NAV = (Total Portfolio Assets - Liabilities) / Outstanding Fund Units
    Ops->>PM: Route calculated NAV to risk/finance for internal audit sign-off (08:30 PM)
    Ops->>Custodian: Uploads validated NAVs to AMFI, AMCs & RTAs (09:00 PM - 10:00 PM cutoff)